{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/objc(cs)NSObject"],"type":"inheritsFrom"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"You can use a HVTCamera object to establish a connection with the device camera, update the attached preview(s)","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and record to an audio\/video container file."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/HVTCameraDelegate","doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/HVTBufferDelegate","doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/HVTView"],"anchor":"Camera","generated":true,"title":"Camera"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HorizonSDK"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HVTCamera","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HVTCamera"}],"title":"HVTCamera","externalID":"c:objc(cs)HVTCamera"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/HVTCamera","interfaceLanguage":"occ"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"@interface"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HVTCamera"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSObject","text":"NSObject"}],"languages":["occ"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/QuickStart","doc:\/\/com.hvt.horizonsdk.framework\/documentation\/HorizonSDK\/Installation"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When HVTcamera is running, it processes the flow of data from the camera device in real time, by utilizing the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internal leveler and applying filters. You can alter the leveler’s settings using the provided properties. Some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties are animated and can be changed even while recording without producing rough transitions in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resulting video.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"####Usage"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple usage scenario of the class requires the following steps in that particular order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate a HVTCamera object."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set the interfaceOrientation property."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(Optional) Implement and set a HVTCameraDelegate object."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want to display the video preview, you can attach one or more HVTView objects by calling addView:."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoke startRunning. Make sure you have handled all the camera & microphone permissions first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoke startRecordingWithMovieURL: to start recording to a QuickTime movie file."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoke stopRecording."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Invoke stopRunning."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"####Camera resolution","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"HVTCamera receives video frames from an AVCaptureDevice instance, which can be accessed by the cameraDevice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property. You can query the supported resolutions using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVCaptureDevice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formats"},{"type":"text","text":" property."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, the resolution used is the one set in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVCaptureDevice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"activeFormat"},{"text":" property. If you want to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set a specific resolution, use one of the methods provided by HVTCamera and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVFoundation"},{"text":"’s methods.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you set the resolution or\/and frame rate while HVTCamera isRunning, the connection to the deviceCamera will be reset,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which can take some time. The call will block until the connection has been established. So set the resolution before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calling startRunning if possible.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"####Performance Considerations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For performance reasons, the maximum supported resolution and frame rate are 1920X1080 and 60 frames\/sec respectively."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In some devices, it is recommended to use a lower resolution. For example, prefer 1280X720 in iPhone 4S."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The use of video filters can significantly impact performance.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/horizonsdk\/hvtcamera"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor"